        "responses": {
          "values": [
            {
              "role": "system",
              "content": "==You are an intent classification and entity extraction engine for a personal task assistant.\n\nToday's date is {{ $now.format('yyyy-MM-dd') }} ({{ $now.format('cccc') }}). Timezone: Asia/Jakarta.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON, no markdown formatting, no code fences, no explanation — just the raw JSON object, in this exact shape:\n{\n  \"intent\": \"create_task\" | \"list_tasks\" | \"create_event\" | \"list_events\" | \"unknown\",\n  \"title\": string or null,\n  \"description\": string or null,\n  \"due_at\": string or null,\n  \"query_date\": string or null\n}\n\nRules:\n- Use \"unknown\" if the message doesn't clearly match one of the other intents.\n- For create_task: title is required. due_at is optional — set it if the user mentioned a deadline or time (this makes it a reminder).\n- For create_event: title and due_at are both required (due_at is the event start time).\n- For list_tasks: title, description, and due_at should all be null.\n- For list_events: title, description, and due_at should all be null. Use this when the user is asking what's on their calendar/schedule, as opposed to asking about their to-do tasks.\n- query_date only applies to list_tasks and list_events. If the user asks about a specific day (\"today\", \"tomorrow\", \"this Friday\", \"on the 15th\"), resolve it into an absolute ISO date (YYYY-MM-DD) using today's date above. If no specific day is mentioned (e.g. plain \"what are my tasks\" or \"what's on my calendar\"), set query_date to null.\n- For create_task, create_event, and unknown, query_date is always null.\n- Resolve relative dates/times (\"Friday at 10am\", \"tomorrow\", \"next week\") into an absolute ISO 8601 datetime (e.g. \"2026-09-11T10:00:00+07:00\") using today's date above."
            },
            {
              "content": "=={{ $('Telegram Trigger').item.json.message.text }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.openAi",
